msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:14
#: 954f5a01be4b4b389dfc428915cfd923
msgid ""
"*qfilexchgd* is a dom0 daemon responsible for managing exchange of block "
"devices (“virtual pendrives”) between VMs. It is used for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:16
#: ae5229604a3a446ebe13a1d46ea1143c
msgid "copying files between AppVMs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:18
#: a6dcd0e04cfd40a3895b76d22b17aabd
msgid "copying a single file between an AppVM and a DisposableVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:22
#: 131c7ae2c0c24abeba3367fb329f0b4c
msgid ""
"*qfilexchgd* is started after first *qubes_guid* has been started, so that "
"it has access to X display in dom0 to present dialog messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:24
#: 2dc3d9eb58bc4c479492111860270ca0
msgid "*qfilexchgd* is event driven. The sources of events are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:26
#: a683566bb3274724bea0362383c3d1d3
msgid ""
"trigger of xenstore watch for the changes in ``/local/domain`` xenstore "
"hierarchy - to detect start/stop of VMs, and maintain vmname->vm_xid "
"dictionary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:28
#: e9c77b981e614f7b99c3fce453c95455
msgid ""
"trigger of xenstore watch for a change in ``/local/domain/domid/device/"
"qpen`` key - VMs write to this key to request service from *qfilexchgd*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:33
#: b8b867e6f14e47df99a07e125115d61e
msgid "Copying files between AppVMs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:36
#: 346bc8757bc54cc38f08218abc90a4e6
msgid ""
"AppVM1 user runs *qvm-copy-to-vm* script (accessible from Dolphin file "
"manager by right click on a file(s): :menuselection:`Actions->Send to VM`). "
"It calls */usr/lib/qubes/qubes_penctl new*, and it writes “new” request to "
"its ``device/qpen`` xenstore key. *qfilexchgd* creates a new 1G file, makes "
"vfat fs on it, and does block-attach so that this file is attached as ``/dev/"
"xvdg`` in AppVM1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:38
#: cb7b1fbb35f644fe9ef80e64b9ca62ea
msgid ""
"AppVM1 mounts ``/dev/xvdg`` on ``/mnt/outgoing`` and copies requested files "
"there, then unmounts it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:40
#: fa681d614aeb4537a770fd5d3edd6bc9
msgid ""
"AppVM1 writes “send DestVM” request to its ``device/qpen`` xenstore key "
"(calling */usr/lib/qubes/qubes_penctl send DestVM*). After getting "
"confirmation by displaying a dialog box in dom0 display, *qfilexchgd* "
"detaches ``/dev/xvdg`` from AppVM1, attaches it as ``/dev/xvdh`` to DestVM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:42
#: f8623038f632426d95d1a645557afd74
msgid ""
"In DestVM, udev script for ``/dev/xvdh`` named *qubes_add_pendrive_script* "
"(see ``/etc/udev/rules.d/qubes.rules``) mounts ``/dev/xvdh`` on ``/mnt/"
"incoming``, and then waits for ``/mnt/incoming`` to become unmounted. A file "
"manager running in DestVM shows a new volume, and user in DestVM may copy "
"files from it. When user in DestVM is done, then user unmounts ``/mnt/"
"incoming``. *qubes_add_pendrive*_script then tells *qfilexchgd* to detach ``/"
"dev/xvdh`` and terminates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:47
#: ac85f2389536407ba5ac2907d7639f53
msgid "Copying a single file between AppVM and a DisposableVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:50
#: fff0c8707ca1419da67833a0c9eceda9
msgid ""
"In order to minimize attack surface presented by necessity to process "
"virtual pendrive metadata sent by (potentially compromised and malicious) "
"DisposableVM, AppVM<->DisposableVM file exchange protocol does not use any "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:52
#: fa666b24dd7b43dea791d97d0393175b
msgid ""
"User in AppVM1 runs *qvm-open-in-dvm* (accessible from Dolphin file manager "
"by right click on a file: :menuselection:`Actions->Open in DisposableVM` "
"menu). *qvm-open-in-dvm*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:54
#: 26e3370730e24467bb386d6b2a9097ac
msgid "gets a new ``/dev/xvdg`` (just as described in previous paragraph)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:56
#: 2eac702a1d3e42778db2cbed6e73bb13
msgid ""
"computes a new unique transaction seq SEQ by incrementing ``/home/user/.dvm/"
"seq`` contents,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:58
#: 44d766fd546d40aa84a0844030939cf2
msgid ""
"writes the requested file name (say, /home/user/document.txt) to ``/home/"
"user/.dvm/SEQ``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:60
#: 86d7ccfd4d3344eca86b9aff210a7a54
msgid ""
"creates a dvm_header (see core.git/appvm/dvm.h) on ``/dev/xvdg``, followed "
"by file contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:62
#: b622a72188a44c5e90b81b3dc27a7273
msgid ""
"writes the “send disposable SEQ” command to its ``device/qpen`` xenstore key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:66
#: 385fb853cf44467cbd88ae5451baa059
msgid ""
"*qfilexchgd* sees that “send” argument==“disposable”, and creates a new "
"DisposableVM by calling */usr/lib/qubes/qubes_restore*. It adds the new "
"DisposableVM to qubesDB via qvm_collection.add_new_disposablevm. Then it "
"attaches the virtual pendrive (previously attached as ``/dev/xvdg`` at "
"AppVM1) as ``/dev/xvdh`` in DisposableVM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:68
#: 4a1dc3fc1faa4fca8bf78ce6e09b736e
msgid ""
"In DisposableVM, *qubes_add_pendrive_script* sees non-zero "
"``qubes_transaction_seq`` key in xenstore, and instead processing the "
"virtual pendrive as in the case of normal copy, treats it as DVM transaction "
"(a request, because we run in DisposableVM). It retrieves the body of the "
"file passed in ``/dev/xvdh``, copies to /tmp, and runs *mime-open* utility "
"to open appropriate executable to edit it. When *mime-open* returns, if the "
"file was modified, it is sent back to AppVM1 (by writing “send AppVM1 SEQ” "
"to ``device/qpen`` xenstore key). Then DisposableVM destroys itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qfileexchgd.rst:70
#: 65d3f7be2344424694fc10e9d1fbe1b2
msgid ""
"In AppVM1, a new ``/dev/xvdh`` appears (because DisposableVM has sent it). "
"*qubes_add_pendrive_script* sees non-zero ``qubes_transaction_seq`` key, and "
"treats it as DVM transaction (a response, because we run in AppVM, not "
"DisposableVM). It retrieves the filename from ``/home/user/.dvm/SEQ``, and "
"copies data from ``/dev/xvdh`` to it."
msgstr ""
